00:16:48.680 --> 00:16:51.200
My question is about
the impact that RStudio

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.690
has had on the community
over the years.

00:16:53.690 --> 00:16:56.900
I think it's been really
positive in helping

00:16:56.900 --> 00:17:01.580
the community be welcoming and
encouraging and open in a way

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.880
that I think folks agree, and
we make lots of jokes about,

00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:07.369
was not necessarily
the way when I was

00:17:07.369 --> 00:17:09.390
a grad student, for example.

00:17:09.390 --> 00:17:11.442
Was that a conscientious
orientation?

00:17:11.442 --> 00:17:12.859
I'm curious about
the story of how

00:17:12.859 --> 00:17:15.920
you came to that kind of
contribution in particular

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:17.839
and how conscientious it was.

00:17:17.839 --> 00:17:19.460
Yeah, I was very
conscientious.

00:17:19.460 --> 00:17:22.640
I definitely think
a lot of us first

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:28.050
encountered the R community
in less friendly mood.

00:17:28.050 --> 00:17:33.530
And I think that was
disappointing, like, wow, it'd

00:17:33.530 --> 00:17:36.170
be great if more people felt
welcome and more people felt

00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:39.050
like they could come in and
ask questions and succeed.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:45.920
But I would credit, primarily,
Hadley for his orientation

00:17:45.920 --> 00:17:46.947
around that.

00:17:46.947 --> 00:17:48.530
For those of you
that know him or have

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.480
heard him talk about
this sort of stuff,

00:17:50.480 --> 00:17:56.030
he is extremely passionate
about inclusiveness,

00:17:56.030 --> 00:18:00.620
and friendliness,
and welcomingness.

00:18:00.620 --> 00:18:02.180
I mean, there's a
lot of people here

00:18:02.180 --> 00:18:03.920
who believe in those things.

00:18:03.920 --> 00:18:07.100
But he really set
the tone for that

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:10.370
and for the whole community
and for the company.

00:18:10.370 --> 00:18:13.322
It's definitely
very self-conscious.

00:18:13.322 --> 00:18:14.280
That's great to hear.

00:18:14.280 --> 00:18:17.320
It's really made an impact.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:18.650
Thanks.

00:18:18.650 --> 00:18:19.620
Thank you.

