00:45:56.070 --> 00:45:57.540
How about just generally?

00:45:57.540 --> 00:45:58.440
Generally?

00:46:05.640 --> 00:46:12.570
I listen to some political
and social commentary stuff.

00:46:12.570 --> 00:46:15.790
I rather listen to some
Magic the Gathering stuff.

00:46:15.790 --> 00:46:18.840
Again, this is all pretty
particular flavored.

00:46:18.840 --> 00:46:21.540
I don't know that I'd make
general recommendations from.

00:46:21.540 --> 00:46:22.260
Let me think.

00:46:26.020 --> 00:46:29.490
I will say that.

00:46:29.490 --> 00:46:35.880
It goes back a little bit to
the question about ChatGBT.

00:46:35.880 --> 00:46:38.400
There is one
organization in podcasts

00:46:38.400 --> 00:46:41.820
that I do listen to,
that I do recommend.

00:46:41.820 --> 00:46:43.950
There's an organization
called the Center

00:46:43.950 --> 00:46:46.410
for Humane Technology.

00:46:46.410 --> 00:46:47.445
And they have a podcast.

00:46:52.560 --> 00:46:56.760
In the '80s and '90s, everyone
was a techno optimist,

00:46:56.760 --> 00:46:58.620
like the more tech the better.

00:46:58.620 --> 00:47:01.230
And then we've seen
in the last 10 years

00:47:01.230 --> 00:47:06.780
how tech that's
developed unreflective

00:47:06.780 --> 00:47:10.440
and not adequately
understood by its creators,

00:47:10.440 --> 00:47:13.320
and not adequately
regulated by government,

00:47:13.320 --> 00:47:18.280
can lead to some very, very
unpleasant consequences.

00:47:18.280 --> 00:47:21.580
So the Humane Tech Podcast
covers some of that ground.

00:47:21.580 --> 00:47:23.880
So I recommend that.

00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:24.690
Looks awesome.

00:47:24.690 --> 00:47:25.560
I appreciate it.

00:47:28.730 --> 00:47:30.410
Yep, that's the podcast.

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:31.760
Awesome.

00:47:31.760 --> 00:47:35.600
I thought you might also
recommend The Chaos Machine.

00:47:35.600 --> 00:47:36.975
I know that was
one that came up.

00:47:36.975 --> 00:47:38.350
And that's when
I recommended--

00:47:38.350 --> 00:47:40.760
And that, actually, I got
from the Humane Tech Podcast.

00:47:40.760 --> 00:47:44.120
There's a very, very good book
called The Chaos Machine which

00:47:44.120 --> 00:47:46.790
is about--

00:47:46.790 --> 00:47:50.390
you can probably all mostly
guess what The Chaos Machine.

00:47:50.390 --> 00:47:55.850
It's modern social media
and how it got that way,

00:47:55.850 --> 00:47:57.600
and what we might be
able to do about it.

